# Backend Docker Build Context Exclusions
#
# WHY THIS FILE MATTERS (Build Speed Issue)
# ------------------------------------------
# Without .dockerignore, Docker sends the ENTIRE directory to the build
# daemon as the "context" before any layer is built.
#
# What was being sent unnecessarily:
#   - __pycache__ directories   → hundreds of .pyc files, changing constantly
#   - .pytest_cache             → test run artifacts
#   - tests/                    → not needed in the production image
#   - .venv / venv              → if you have a local virtualenv
#   - *.pyc files               → compiled bytecode
#
# Impact: A large context means Docker can't determine if the "COPY ."
# layer changed without hashing everything. Even if you only changed one
# .py file, a big context causes a slow context upload + layer re-eval.
#
# FIX: Exclude all non-runtime files. Docker context drops from ~500MB
# (with a local venv) to ~100KB. Layer caching becomes much more reliable.

__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local virtualenvs
.venv
venv
env

# Test files are not needed in the production image
tests/

# Git and IDE
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# Docs and local notes
*.md
architecture.png
